WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.806
Forty-six Members of Parliament voted for both MAID expansion and the Emergencies Act.

00:00:04.806 --> 00:00:07.000
That is one hundred percent overlap.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.022
The same legislators who authorized state-administered death also authorized the suspension of civil liberties under the Emergencies Act.

00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:22.579
Of those forty-six, five also appear on the Top 50 Most Lobbied Officials list: Maloney, Sgro, Dabrusin, Sarai, and Duguid.

00:00:22.579 --> 00:00:26.534
Three hundred and thirty-eight Members of Parliament voted on the Emergencies Act.

00:00:26.534 --> 00:00:32.999
The convergence matrix maps every MP who authorized both lethal state policy and emergency state control.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.681
This is not correlation.

00:00:34.681 --> 00:00:43.181
This is the same people making the same category of decision — expanding state power over life and liberty — across multiple legislative instruments.

00:00:43.181 --> 00:00:44.840
The pattern is consistent.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.556
The names are documented.
